# Vault git attributes — see notes/vault-multi-machine-sync.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings. Normalize to LF *in the repository* regardless of what any
# individual machine has set for core.autocrlf. Working-tree endings are left
# to the platform default (Windows checkouts still get CRLF via autocrlf=true).
#
# Verified 2026-08-26: every committed blob is already LF, so this is pure
# insurance against a future clone with different settings — NOT a
# renormalization. Without it, a machine with core.autocrlf=false can commit
# CRLF blobs, and the next merge conflicts on *every line of every file*.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Append-only logs: union merge concatenates both sides instead of conflicting.
# Caveat — union does not sort, so entries from two machines can interleave out
# of date order and duplicate a heading. Always eyeball these after a merge.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVED — do not hand-merge. tags/*.md and tags/_index.md are generated from
# each page's `## Tags` section. On conflict take EITHER side and re-derive:
#   py -3 tools/vault-tagindex.py --write   # then
#   py -3 tools/tag-counts.py --write
# (Deliberately not given a merge driver: `merge=ours` would need per-machine
# `git config merge.ours.driver true`, which silently no-ops on a fresh clone.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Binary assets — never diff or line-ending-convert.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.wav  binary
*.zip  binary
*.nes  binary
*.mss  binary
*.dmp  binary
